# Roadmap delivery loop

Read the delivery-loop section of `AGENTS.md`, `CHECKS_LEDGER.md`, and the
plain-English PR skill. These requirements apply together; a new task or rule
does not cancel earlier requirements. Keep docs, schema, examples, evidence,
and implementation consistent throughout review fixes.

Within owner-authorized roadmap work, implement one focused task, verify it,
open a PR using the repo template, and monitor CI and review threads. Fix valid
findings, rerun checks, reply with the fix and evidence, and resolve addressed
threads. Explain invalid findings before resolving them. Never close a thread
merely to make the PR look ready.

Before merging, refresh the PR head, base, checks, reviews, and comments. Resolve
conflicts without discarding either side's intent. Require all applicable checks
to pass and every actionable comment to be addressed; skipped checks are not
proof of coverage. Merge dependency PRs first, target `main` on `origin`, verify
the merge remotely, then continue the next roadmap task.

Example: a reviewer finds that a null trace ID aborts import. Reproduce it, fix
the mapper, add a regression test, pass the required checks, push, reply with
the commit/test, and resolve that thread. Recheck CI and new comments before
merging. Do not resolve it just because a fix has been planned.

Retain the free, open-source, runner-agnostic offline core and honest STATUS.
Keep assistant-ui parked. Under the owner's 2026-11-02 standing instruction,
release coherent portable 0.x milestones after reviewed green merges. Follow
`docs/npm-publishing.md`: verify main, publish through the existing OIDC path,
inspect raw logs and verify registry/tag/installed consumers. Record scope and
evidence. Do not bump for every PR, docs-only change or private hosted slice.
Example: completed portable M1 supports 0.11.0; a README correction alone does
not require another package release. The explicit 1.0.0 and hosted-deployment
owner gates remain separate.
